  "query_preview": "..\nThough benign conditions will continue overnight, anticipate a \nshift to the weather starting mid-day Thursday continuing into \nFriday. Rain will become likely across the ID panhandle and far \nsoutheastern WA, with lesser chances the farther west you go \ninto central WA. Though not as moist, central WA will not be \nleft out completely as gusty winds will develop in these areas\nThursday evening into Friday. In particular, portions of the \nOkanogan Valley, Waterville Plateau, Wenatchee area, Upper \nColumbia Basin, and the northeast Blue Mountains could see gusts\nof 30 to 45 mph. This will also result in elevated fire weather\nconditions and the potential for patchy blowing dust. Winds \nwill decrease friday night. Temps for Friday and the weekend \nwill also be notably cooler than what we're experiencing today \nand Thursday. \n\nIn an unsettled pattern, chances (generally in the 10-30% range)\nfor precipitation will return from Saturday night into early \nnext week. Confidence remains low in the finer details of any\nprecip location and intensity, but those across the Inland \nNorthwest should expect the periodic potential for showers along\nwith seasonably cool temps. KD",
